# Search visibility — read by ripgrep, VS Code, and agent search tools. NOT by git.
#
# .gitignore hides /projects/* so product repos stay independent (ADR-0001). That
# same rule makes product code invisible to every gitignore-aware search tool, which
# breaks the "open your editor at the workspace root" rule this workspace is built on.
#
# This file re-includes the product repos for SEARCH ONLY. Git isolation is untouched:
# `git check-ignore projects/<key>` still reports it ignored and `git add -A` still
# refuses to embed them. `ws doctor` verifies both.
!projects/*/

# Re-including a directory also lifts the default skip on everything inside it, so
# put the noise back. Last matching rule wins, hence the order. Use ** and not *:
# a single * does not match here once the parent has been whitelisted.
projects/**/.git/
projects/**/target/
projects/**/build/
projects/**/node_modules/
projects/**/*.jar

# context/ is ignored by git but is exactly what agents must read: memory, runs,
# the registry, domain skills. Keep it searchable.
!context/
context/**/.git/

# Client material is never searched, whatever a tool's defaults are.
.local/

# Agent tools' own state at the root: run metadata, preview logs, worktree
# metadata. Git already ignores these (see .gitignore); this keeps their logs
# and scratch files out of the search index too.
.freebuff/
.kilo/
.wrangler/

# The Agent-Workspace mirror under projects/ duplicates this repository's own
# instruction payload (AGENTS.md, .agents/, docs/, editor rules). Indexing both
# copies double-counts every instruction file and inflates agent context; keep
# only the original in the search index. The mirror stays fully readable by
# explicit path, and its product code under projects/ is untouched.
projects/donwi/public/Agent-Workspace/AGENTS.md
projects/donwi/public/Agent-Workspace/CLAUDE.md
projects/donwi/public/Agent-Workspace/GEMINI.md
projects/donwi/public/Agent-Workspace/.agents/
projects/donwi/public/Agent-Workspace/docs/
projects/donwi/public/Agent-Workspace/.cursor/
projects/donwi/public/Agent-Workspace/.github/
projects/donwi/public/Agent-Workspace/.vscode/
projects/donwi/public/Agent-Workspace/apps/
